_meanings:
Rather or better than, preferably to, it is better
 that <ab>&c.</ab> It is sometimes used with the ablative; {#samunnayan BUtimanAryasaMgamAdvaraM#}
 {#viroDo'pi samaM mahAtmaBiH#} <ls>Ki. 1. 8</ls>. But it is generally used absolutely,
 {#varam#} being used with the clause containing the thing preferred, and
 {#na ca, na tu#}, or {#na punaH#} with the clause containing the thing
 to which the first is preferred, (both being put in the nominative case);
 {#varaM mOnaM kAryaM na ca vacanamuktaM yadanftaM … varaM BikzASitvaM#}
 {#na ca paraDanAsvAdanasuKam#} <ls>H. 1. 116</ls>; {#varaM prARatyAgo na punaraDamAnAmupagamaH#}
 {%<ab>ibid.</ab>%}; {#varaM garBasrAvo varamftuzu nEvABigamanam, varaM jAtapreto#}
 {#varamapi ca kanyEva janitA . varaM vanDyA BAryA varamapi ca garBezu vasatirna#}
 {#cAvidvAn rUpadraviRaguRayukto'pi tanayaH ..#} <ls>Pt.</ls>; sometimes {#na#} is
 used without {#ca, tu#} or {#punaH#}; {#yAcYA moGA varamaDiguRe nADame labDakAmA#} <ls>Me. 6</ls>.
